      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 1880s, Independence earned the nickname “Lexington of the North” for its horse‑racing boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Wapsipinicon Mill, built in 1867, later supplied electricity to the town from 1915 to 1940.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s Independence State Hospital, a historic mental hospital, sits on a remote tract west of town.",
